text:


A bird is not afraid, for he has wings;

The tiger is not proud, for his claws are sharp;

And I have come here to tell you this:

Don't be afraid!

O, come and let us worship there;
The virgin Mary now is found,

That mother’s blessing gives to me;
A child she holds who hath no sound ;

I have been told, my little child, that thou hast read

The volumes which are written on thy infant mind; —

And knowest that there is nothing but thy God alone;

That He created all things out of His own love ;

To be their joy and not their torment to them prove ;

All beauty from Him came ; all goodness springs from Him ;
